                    [51] Counsel for Tarion pointed out, quite correctly in my view, that the administrative regime for decision making under which Tarion operates is more formal than the administrative regime under which Ontario <b>Employment Standards Act</b>, R.S.O. 1990, c. E.14 (“ESA”) officers operate. ESA officers make decisions in a very &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;[<b>97</b>] I agree with this paragraph. I, therefore, would not give effect to this last prong in Newport’s argument. 
