                    (This decision holds that although the literal reading of the words in the <b>Employment Standards Act</b> entitling an employee to severance, termination or vacation pay upon termination by the employer would not include the employer's bankruptcy, when the words are examined in their entire context they must be interpreted to &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;[<b>97</b>] Article 16 of Schneider simply states that the certificate is to be delivered to "the transfer agent". 
